        <h2>What the document says about medications. Not a reconciled list — and we say so.</h2>
        <p>Every medication a document mentions, verified against the source. Click a drug, land on that line of the PDF.</p>
        <p>The list appears only in <strong>Review Required</strong>, never on the problem view — under a problem list it would read as <em>the current regimen</em>, and it’s one document’s snapshot, possibly months stale. One Dismiss clears the group, per user and reversibly.</p>
        <p>There’s no Accept button, on purpose: it would imply a write to a reconciled medication list that doesn’t happen.</p>
        {/* NEW COPY, not from the v1 deck — added on Jacob's correction that medications
            have an Include in note path. Needs sign-off, and the attribution label below
            should be checked against the app's actual UI string. */}
        <p><strong>What you can do is use them.</strong> <em>Include in note</em> puts the list into your note, attributed <em>from external records</em> — the same explicit click as every other outside fact.</p>
      </div>
