<!-- S8 — PROPOSED TASKS -->
<section class="s-output ir" id="s8">
  <div class="ic">
    <div class="output-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="il">OUTPUT 3 — PROPOSED TASKS</div>
        <h2>Three real follow-ups, not thirty plausible ones.</h2>
        <p>Only what the document actually asks for — <em>“Repeat BMP in 1–2 weeks”</em>, <em>“Refer to cardiology for stress echo”</em> — each with its problem and <strong>the exact quote that justifies it</strong>. Timeframes come verbatim, or stay empty. We don’t invent urgency.</p>
        <p><strong>The quality bar is the feature.</strong> No quote, no task. Ongoing medications, boilerplate, plan summaries and duplicates are left out, and for many documents the right answer is an empty list.</p>
        <p><strong>Nothing is created behind your back.</strong> Accept, edit or delete, then one Save commits it, with a conflict check between reviewers. Accepted tasks go to a named assignee.</p>
        <p><strong>The document itself is somebody’s job.</strong> Every confirmed document creates a review task for a named clinician, so a 4pm fax isn’t in a queue nobody owns.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mock">
        <div class="mock-marker">Demo — fake patient data — not a real chart</div>
